      "finalExcerpt": "`parse_price(\"1,234.50\")` now returns `1234.5`, and all 5 tests pass. But `mis verdict` says **PARTIAL**, not VERIFIED, because the quality review is missing.\n\n**The fix**\n- `inventory.py` now treats commas as thousands separators when a three-digit comma group is followed by a dot (`1,234.50`) or b\n…\n the run, so the corrected review was refused and nothing was recorded.\n- To get VERIFIED, run the quality review against the current code in a fresh run, for example with `/make-it-ship:review`.\n\n**What I did without asking**\n- Because you said to proceed without questions, I wrote the proposed `.make-it-ship.json` with the single `unit` check and ran in Quick mode.\n- That config file is now in the repo as an uncommitted change, alongside the edits to `inventory.py` and `tests/test_inventory.py`. I haven't committed anything.\n\nThe report is at `docs/make-it-ship/20261021-1345-9d29/report.md`.",
